{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1369231-new-legacy-the-karmic-equation","id":1369231,"title":"[New Legacy] The Karmic Equation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-20T17:07:12-08:00","id":1369231,"title":"[New Legacy] The Karmic Equation","content":"Author's note: the format for this Legacy is borrowed from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2757_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2757\" data-vbnamecard=\"2757\">proindrakenzol</a>.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Murder and similarly heinous crimes have a marked tendency to upset the equilibrium between the worlds of the living and dead. Not only that, they often attract those who wish to solve them but lack the necessary knowledge. The members of this Legacy intervene in criminal cases that serve as the focal points for significant ghostly activity, employing arcane methodologies focused on altering destinies with surgical precision. By enacting justice and tying up loose ends, they allow ghosts to pass on and prevent the living from delving too far into unsolved mysteries.<br /> <br /> Origins<br /> Parentage: Acanthus, Guardians Of The Veil<br /> Nicknames: Psychopomps<br /> Background: Private investigators, police officers and occultists with a desire to guide the hand of karma via necromantic practices.<br /> Nimbus: A pair of scales made out of bones hovers above the Mage's head like a halo.<br /> <br /> Doctrine<br /> Prerequisites: Death 2, Investigation 2, Occult 2, a Specialty for Numerology or other appropriate field, Allies 1 (Sin Eaters)<br /> Initiation: One must find an unsolved crime that has resulted in a major haunting, use numerology or other appropriate field to arrange a perfect sequence of events that brings the culprit to justice (legal or poetic) and then bring closure to the unfinished business of the victim's ghost.<br /> <br /> Organization: Psychopomps organize themselves analogously to a department of law enforcement, with each member combining their mundane talents and arcane knowledge to cover multiple methods of investigation. One might deal with interviewing ghosts, a second analyzes the crime scene and a third secures the area from intrusion and tampering. Krewes of Sin-Eaters are considered adjunct consultants as a matter of practicality and tradition. Not only that, they are known for displaying a Holmes-Watson dynamic when training initiates, similarly to the Eleventh Question. Lastly, they are frequently hired by Consilia to deal with Reaper-Mages, and become trusted sources of knowledge on this matter.<br /> <br /> Magic<br /> Ruling Arcanum: Death<br /> Yantras: Forensic equipment and criminal evidence (+1), badges of authority and trophies of exemplary service (+1), succeeding on an Investigation or Occult roll relevant to the spell (+2), mementos from haunted locations whose ghostly entities have passed on with your help (+2)<br /> Oblations: Meticulously planning for an investigation via numerology or other appropriate field, interviewing and cooperating with ghostly entities, personally hearing out the confessions or justifications of criminals before delivering them to justice<br /> <br /> Attainments<br /> <br /> First: Probabilistic Forensics<br /> Prerequisite: Initiation<br /> The Mage knows how to look for the typical signs of ghostly activity. This works like Soul Marks, with Reach assigned to Instant Casting.<br /> Optional: Fate 1<br /> The Mage notices the clues that might link together victim and culprit. This works like Interconnections, with Reach assigned to Instant Casting.<br /> <br /> Second: Algebraic Necromancy<br /> Prerequisite: Death 2, either Investigation 3 or Occult 3<br /> The Mage prepares a seance for the dead to communicate with the living. This works like Speak With The Dead, which is cast as a Ritual and has Reach assigned to Advanced Duration and Advanced Scale [Subjects]. The amount of subjects must be divided between the living and dead participants.<br /> Optional: Fate 2<br /> The Mage receives a glimpse of what he is meant to do in other to progress in his investigations. This works like Serendipity, with Reach assigned to Instant Casting and Advanced Duration.<br /> <br /> Third: Phantasmagorical Deduction<br /> Prerequisite: Death 3, both Investigation 3 and Occult 3<br /> The Mage cloaks himself in a deathly shroud, allowing him to better investigate suspects without being discovered. This works like Ghost Gate, with Reach assigned to Instant Casting. Of note is that the Duration refers to the gateway. The Mage remains in Twilight until he goes through the gateway again.<br /> Optional: Fate 3<br /> The Mage controls probability so that he &quot;coincidentally&quot; comes across evidence and clues related to the crime. This works like Shifting The Odds, which is cast as a Ritual and has Reach assigned to Advanced Duration and higher specificity. For example: he could not only find a murderer, but also one who is suffering from the Paranoia Condition and has Status 3+ (Mafia).<br /> <br /> Fourth: Fatal Miscalculation<br /> Prerequisite: Death 4, Investigation 4 and Occult 3, or Investigation 3 and Occult 4<br /> The Mage reveals to the suspect exactly just how much harm they've caused and compels their cooperation. This works like Judgment (see below), with Reach assigned to Instant Casting, Advanced Duration, vision of last moments and Exceptional Success with 3 Successes.<br /> Optional: Fate 4<br /> The Mage conceals the meaning of his investigations so as to appear like he is meant to be there. This works like Unseen Hands (see below), with Reach assigned to Instant Casting, Advanced Duration and inflicting the Misinformed Condition.<br /> <br /> Fifth: Elegant Solution<br /> Prerequisite: Death 5, both Investigation 4 and Occult 4<br /> The Mage will not tolerate the absence of justice and his retribution is swift. This is a Death Making spell, which immediately kills the target, eliminates all possible Manifestation Conditions of their ghost and sends them directly to the Underworld. If the target is a ghostly entity, all their current Manifestation Conditions are eliminated and they are sent to the Underworld just the same. Reach is assigned to Instant Casting.<br /> Optional: Fate 5<br /> The Mage is not utterly without mercy and can arrange opportunities for both victim and culprit to reach an understanding and make amends. This works like Atonement, which is cast as a Ritual and has Reach assigned to Advanced Duration and allowing the quest to be undertaken on the subject's behalf by another. The ghost receives guidance on how to move on, and the murderer can be given a chance to deal with his guilt and heal from the torment the ghost inflicted on him. If the culprit is incapable or unwilling to atone for whatever reason, one of their loved ones or allies can take on the burden of atonement for them.<br /> <br /> Judgment (Death \u2022)<br /> Practice: Unveiling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Withstood: Composure<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Investigation, Persuasion, Intimidation<br /> The Mage forces a vision upon the target which clearly reveals the gravity of all harmful actions they have performed within the Duration of the spell. Harmful actions are defined here as those which caused damage, negative Conditions or Tilts, and Breaking Points. The target of the spell suffers the Guilty Condition.<br /> +1 Reach: If the target's actions have resulted in someone's death, the Mage receives a brief vision of the victim's last moments. This grants [Potency] bonus dice on Perception rolls to find them for the spell's Duration.<br /> +1 Reach, 1 Mana: If the Mage takes advantage of the Guilty Condition, he achieves Exceptional Success with 3 Successes.<br /> <br /> Unseen Hands (Fate \u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Veiling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Withstood: Composure<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Stealth, Subterfuge, Persuasion<br /> For the Duration of the spell, any actions the Mage takes which could be considered strange or invasive are considered routine parts of everyone's lives. Others will not find evidence to the contrary via mundane means unless they are specifically looking for the Mage, and supernatural means of investigation trigger a Clash Of Wills.<br /> +1 Reach, 1 Mana: The Mage redirects any possible suspicion toward false leads and scapegoats. If someone manages to suspect that something is not right about the Mage's actions, they suffer the Misinformed Condition on a number of rolls equal to [Potency] to find evidence for it.<br /> <br /> Misinformed<br /> Effect: You've gathered or been given extensive but misleading information. When making a roll for the relevant topic, you may Resolve this Condition to gain a Beat. Your result is downgraded by one step (Exceptional Success =&gt; Baseline Success =&gt; Baseline Failure =&gt; Dramatic Failure). Should you get a Dramatic Failure, you receive another Beat.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-24-2020, 10:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T10:13:36-08:00","id":1369399,"title":"","content":"Detectives specializing in putting the dead at rest, with a natural synergy towards Geists, its a very cool idea.<br /> <br /> But I have to ask, why is the parent Order the Guardians of the Veil ? I could see detective noir resonating with the Free Council, the Silver Ladder seeing their work as a type of final rites, part of their duties. The Arrow would consider resolving the grief of those passed as a path towards honor (the Mysterium would probably prefer Stone Scribes). The Eleventh Question are in the Order as the exception that proves the rule, sometimes you need investigators in a society of spies, to efficiently expose trouble before it snowballs into a catastrophic violation of the Veil. But ghosts, spirits and ethereal entities do not necessarily expose the Veil and don't cause Paradox.<br /> <br /> Regarding the nickname, its the same as the Exarch that wants to prevent souls from moving on. That might raise all sorts of red flags, even if their intention is to do the opposite than the Tyrant.<br /> <br /> For the second optional Attainment, it could allow substituting a mental skill for Occult or Investigation, but only regarding ghosts or murder cases. This would allow them to, for example, use numerology to figure out the political goal of the hired killer's contractor or use occult patterns to puzzle out the components of the rare poison in the deadly dart.<br /> <br /> The last Attainments reminds me of the Ghost Rider's Penance Stare, maybe it could leave some clues like carbonized eyes or the smell of the rivers of the Underworld. These serve no real purpose beyond stylistic.<br /> <br /> Since the last main Attainment rules out vengeance plots and dangerous ghosts, have you considered using the optional one to give the ghost a chance to set things right ? For example, it figures out the conditions and gives them a choice: it allow them to Manifest, but it ends if they stop working towards the goals for Atonement. So a wife would get a chance to say goodbye to her murdered husband, the athlete would get to play for his team one last time, which paired with Unseen Hands means they will only realize it later. This could lead to some urban legends of ghostly miracles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-21-2020, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T10:47:21-08:00","id":1369407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1369231-new-legacy-the-karmic-equation?p=1369399#post1369399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Detectives specializing in putting the dead at rest, with a natural synergy towards Geists, its a very cool idea.<br /> <br /> But I have to ask, why is the parent Order the Guardians of the Veil ? I could see detective noir resonating with the Free Council, the Silver Ladder seeing their work as a type of final rites, part of their duties. The Arrow would consider resolving the grief of those passed as a path towards honor (the Mysterium would probably prefer Stone Scribes). The Eleventh Question are in the Order as the exception that proves the rule, sometimes you need investigators in a society of spies, to efficiently expose trouble before it snowballs into a catastrophic violation of the Veil. But ghosts, spirits and ethereal entities do not necessarily expose the Veil and don't cause Paradox.<br /> <br /> Regarding the nickname, its the same as the Exarch that wants to prevent souls from moving on. That might raise all sorts of red flags, even if their intention is to do the opposite than the Tyrant.<br /> <br /> For the second optional Attainment, it could allow substituting a mental skill for Occult or Investigation, but only regarding ghosts or murder cases. This would allow them to, for example, use numerology to figure out the political goal of the hired killer's contractor or use occult patterns to puzzle out the components of the rare poison in the deadly dart.<br /> <br /> The last Attainments reminds me of the Ghost Rider's Penance Stare, maybe it could leave some clues like carbonized eyes or the smell of the rivers of the Underworld. These serve no real purpose beyond stylistic.<br /> <br /> Since the last main Attainment rules out vengeance plots and dangerous ghosts, have you considered using the optional one to give the ghost a chance to set things right ? For example, it figures out the conditions and gives them a choice: it allow them to Manifest, but it ends if they stop working towards the goals for Atonement. So a wife would get a chance to say goodbye to her murdered husband, the athlete would get to play for his team one last time, which paired with Unseen Hands means they will only realize it later. This could lead to some urban legends of ghostly miracles.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you for the feedback! In order of your observations:<br /> <br /> I chose the Guardians instead of Arrows mostly because I wanted it to be distinct from my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1300727-new-legacy-phagocytes\"><b>Phagocytes</b>.</a> Also because the Guardians seemed like a natural fit for a Legacy with such a strong focus on surgical retribution. But in all honesty, it's an approximation. Feel free to replace Guardians with another Order if you really want to.<br /> <br /> I had forgotten the Death Exarch was called that. I'll think about a new nickname for them. How about <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moirai\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Moirai?</b></a><br /> <br /> Your suggestion for the second Fate Attainment makes sense, but I figure they can just cast Serendipity as a normal spell so they can pull off that trick. I also figure most of them have Numerology or equivalent field as an Interdisciplinary Specialty.<br /> <br /> Those are totally fitting cosmetic details for the last Death Attainment, yes. And those scenarios you imagined for the final Fate Attainment are totally in-character, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 02-21-2020, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T16:37:04-08:00","id":1369469,"title":"","content":"I think Moirai overlaps with the Thread Cutters, how about Tarakas ? That carries the symbolism of Shiva as a psychopomp that guides souls towards moksha and beyond the cycle of suffering. That way the main and optional fifth Attainment complete that path in different ways. <br /> <br /> I think that restricting the Serendipity bonus might help give the feel of a predestined intervention, a hard boiled detective charged with authority by fate, so things just work out in accordance to their esoteric ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-21-2020, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}